    "body": "The learned #1077 reader and frozen compound-binding core had not been qualified together through R4. This adds token-to-clause transport for all 15 learned soft role mixtures, then reuses the existing full four-fact-plus-null R4 attention. Both learned artifacts, ordinary contextual scoring and native geometry stay fixed.\n\nThe sole campaign preserves all 25,600 answers and 358,400 supervised role decisions across six observed views; all 156 preservation criteria pass. Maximum full-head difference is 8.82149e-6. Fact-frame corruption causes 84.18–93.26 percentage-point supported loss in every view. Token-frame corruption causes 28.72–52.64 points and meets the frozen strong-sensitivity threshold in only three of six views. The recorded terminal is LANGUAGE_R4_PRESERVED_CONTROL_WEAK: retain preservation and the strong fact-control result, then separately diagnose construction-only, attention-weighted token-frame exposure with the model and control fixed.\n\nOne fresh-process replay reproduces the complete evidence exactly. Combined run/replay: 57.0422 seconds, peak 2.2171 GiB, four CPU threads. Twelve focused adapter/provenance/decision checks, Ruff and claim wording pass. No training, new populations, hard-field oracle forwards, geometry expansion, native exports or generation. Broad QA remains NOT_RUN; protected-queue acknowledgements transport the reviewed content and are not test evidence.\n\nThe append-only record and exact preparation/result/replay envelopes are in docs/r4_zoology_language_r4_1079*. Six current project mirrors carry the measured result and next diagnostic. #973 remains open and #954 blocked. References #1079; issue closure follows verified merge and native tracker updates.\n",
